Straight-Through Cable: Used to connect different devices (e.g., PC to Switch, Switch to Router). Uses the T568B standard on both ends.

Crossover Cable: Used to connect similar devices (e.g., PC to PC, Switch to Switch, Router to Router). Uses T568A on one end and T568B on the other.

T568B Color Code: White/Orange, Orange, White/Green, Blue, White/Blue, Green, White/Brown, Brown.

Experiment 2: Study of Basic Network Commands
Note: This is done on a real computer or inside the Packet Tracer PC Command Prompt.
Theory & Common Commands:

ipconfig: Displays the IP address, Subnet Mask, and Default Gateway of the PC.

ping <IP>: Tests connectivity to another device (sends ICMP packets).

tracert <IP>: Traces the exact path (routers) a packet takes to reach a destination.

arp -a: Shows the ARP cache (MAC addresses mapped to IP addresses).

nslookup <website>: Queries DNS to find the IP address of a domain name.

Experiment 3: Study and Installation of Various Network Devices
Note: This is a reading/theory lab.
Key Devices to know:

Hub: Old technology. Broadcasts data to all ports (causes collisions).

Switch: Layer 2 device. Uses MAC addresses to send data only to the intended device.

Router: Layer 3 device. Connects different networks together and finds the best path (routing).

Firewall: Blocks unauthorized access.

Access Point: Connects wireless devices to a wired network.

